From ceddc668207b8bb787ae2247ffb4939fdac7f459 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:39:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] umbp: optional driver-pinned DRAM pool (UMBP_DRAM_PINNED=1)

The DRAM tier is anonymous memory registered whole with hipHostRegister. The kernel may still
migrate those pages (compaction); the GPU driver tracks them as userptr and, after any migration,
evicts every GPU queue of the process until the whole region is revalidated -- minutes for a
400+ GiB tier, during which the server answers nothing. With UMBP_DRAM_PINNED=1 the pool comes
from hipHostMalloc (Portable | Mapped | NonCoherent), which is never migrated; registration then
only records the device aliases.

Signed-off-by: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
